INTERPRETATION
For r=j-s, the exact binomial ratio is

  binom(2j+1,2s) / binom(2j+1,2r) = (2s+1)/(2r+1).

The corresponding one-to-one reflected pair can be negative.  Its
cumulative reflected tail can also be negative, and the tail after the
proved t=3 prefix can be negative.  Therefore none of these three
reductions proves the full prefix.  The lower-half slices tested in the
same scan remain nonnegative, consistently with the K_s conjecture.

